WORK SESSIONS

This folder holds one record per work session: what was asked, what got
done, what failed, and what comes next. The main purpose is recall and
handoff. An AI agent starting work in this repository should be able to
read the newest record and carry on without asking Fred to repeat himself.


WHY THIS REPLACES DOCS/AI

Since 2026-11-17, tam-pane uses work/ instead of docs/ai/, as a trial. If
it works better, it will be used across Tamlinux.

docs/ai/ recorded the useful things: Fred's prompts, commit hashes, test
results and the reasons behind choices. Those are kept here. But it also
turned into paperwork. Every session edited an index file and two tables
as well as its record, and every record repeated the same boilerplate
fields. Agents made commits only to write a record's own hash into it, or
to refresh an index; in tam, about one commit in ten did nothing else.
docs/ai/ also had no place for failures or a handoff, which are what the
next agent needs most.

So these records are short and plain, nothing indexes them, and the
record goes in a commit with the work.


THE PROCEDURE

At the start of a session, read this file and then the newest record:

    ls work | sort -V | tail -1

Its HANDOFF section is the current to-do list.

At the end of a session, write one record and commit it with the work
(or with the session's last commit). If the session goes on after that,
update the same record instead of starting another.

Any HANDOFF item from the previous record that is still open is repeated
in the new record, so the newest record is the only place to look.


NAMING

Name each record W<number>-<name>, with no extension and no date: for
example W3-lua-5-5. The number gives the order. The date goes inside the
record, because git sets every file's date to when it was checked out.


FORMAT

Plain text, no Markdown, lines no longer than 76 characters. One value per
header line. Section names in capitals.

    W3 LUA 5.5, AND WORK RECORDS REPLACE DOCS/AI

    Date: 2026-11-17
    AI harness: Claude Code 2.1.326
    AI model: claude-opus-5-5
    Commits: e8a8f38, 68be547
    Continues: W2  (only when this session picked up W2's handoff)

    GUIDANCE

      Fred: "Use lua 5.5 for tam-pane. Update that repo."

    DONE

      - What changed and how it was checked, one item per change.

    FAILED

      - What was tried and did not work, and why. "Nothing." if nothing.

    HANDOFF

      - What is left, in the order to do it. "None." if nothing.

Rules:

  - Take the harness version from the running tool (claude --version,
    codex --version), never from memory.
  - Commits lists the work's commits. A record never contains the hash of
    the commit that adds it, and no commit is made just to add a hash.
  - Continues names the record whose handoff this session picked up. Leave
    it out otherwise.
  - Quote Fred's prompts that steered the work, word for word. Leave out
    side remarks.
  - Write only what the next agent needs and cannot get from the diff.
    15 to 40 lines is typical.


PRIVACY

This repository is public. Records never contain session IDs, transcript
or store paths, home-directory paths, private repository names or private
decision numbers. Transcripts are kept privately by the author; one
private line per record maps it to its transcript.

Commits made with AI help still carry Co-authored-by, AI-Tool (with the
version) and AI-Model trailers.
